{"availability":"available","full":"guilyx/grip","name":"grip","description":"keep a grip!","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":9,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-20T22:49:36Z","updated":"2026-10-09T09:35:45Z","license":"BSD-3-Clause","branch":"main","homepage":"https://guilyx.github.io/grip/","topics":[],"demo":"https://guilyx.github.io/grip/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:04:02.012Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T19:04:02.012Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T19:04:02.012Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:04:02.012Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"x","name":"As Seen On X.com","url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2108158779581984930","postId":"2108158779581984930","postedAt":"2026-10-08T11:33:15.000Z"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T19:04:02.012Z","stars":9,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Keep a grip on your code. grip is a git hook that quizzes you about your own diff before you commit or push it. Five questions, a Grip Score out of 100, and a pass mark you choose. Below the mark, nothing goes upstream.","Generated code, big refactors, late-night pastes: it is easy to ship a change you could not explain in a code review. grip makes you explain it before it leaves your machine. It is a lightweight forcing function, not a gate for correctness: the model asks about behaviour, motivation, edge cases, risks and verification, and grades your answers against a rubric it wrote from the diff.","The gap grip aims at is measured, not imagined. In METR's 2025 randomised trial, experienced open-source developers using AI tools were 19% slower while believing they were 20% faster. GitClear's analysis of 153 million changed lines found code churn on track to double since AI assistants arrived. The 2024 DORA report linked higher AI adoption to lower delivery stability, and the 2025 Stack Overflow survey put developer trust in AI output at a low. Every one of these tools checks the code. grip is the only one that checks the human."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guilyx/grip/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3064daa3ce09e1c7926e63a68c86ba2552338a4e559cd607de2a07b4f8c912a2","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T07:22:00.988Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:04:02.012Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Keep a grip on your code. grip is a git hook that quizzes you about your own diff before you commit or push it. Five questions, a Grip Score out of 100, and a pass mark you choose. Below the mark, nothing goes upstream.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guilyx/grip/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Otherwise grip talks to Anthropic by default: export ANTHROPICAPIKEY (or run ant auth login).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guilyx/grip/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"3064daa3ce09e1c7926e63a68c86ba2552338a4e559cd607de2a07b4f8c912a2","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guilyx/grip/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T19:04:02.012Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T09:35:45Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guilyx/grip/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T19:04:02.012Z","hash":"3064daa3ce09e1c7926e63a68c86ba2552338a4e559cd607de2a07b4f8c912a2","originalBytes":10672,"storedBytes":10672,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["grip","score","push","git","questions","diff","provider","quiz","code","commit","docs","bash","five","model","one","pre-push","agent","pre-commit","runs","what","answers","anthropic","assets","before","codex","gemini","hook","hours","install","launch","mark","pass","skip","about","api","claude","each","explain","grip.toml","keep","passed","writes","add","after","against","answer","any","blocked","cli","cursor","demo","diff.","exclude","fail","generated","grades","hooks","key","license","max","ollama","only","openai","passing","plugin","push.","real","see","text","they","through","toml","to